<wpf:ResourceDictionary xml:space="preserve" xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml" xmlns:s="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib" xmlns:ss="urn:shemas-jetbrains-com:settings-storage-xaml" xmlns:wpf="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation">
	<!--
	  ReSharper InspectCode noise-floor.

	  `jb inspectcode` is run with no explicit profile argument, so it auto-loads
	  this solution-shared layer (the file must be named
	  <SolutionFileName>.DotSettings and sit next to the solution).

	  POLICY: an entry belongs here ONLY when the code is correct and the
	  inspection is WRONG about it. A finding that is merely inconvenient,
	  stylistic, or "accepted" is fixed instead. Every entry below states the
	  evidence that makes it a false positive, and that evidence is reproducible.

	  Everything else InspectCode reported on this repo was FIXED, not silenced —
	  RedundantCast, RedundantNameQualifier, RedundantUsingDirective,
	  RedundantTypeArgumentsOfMethod, xUnit1030, InvalidXmlDocComment,
	  CheckNamespace, S1186/S3237/ValueParameterNotUsed, S108, MA0047,
	  UnusedVariable and one always-true guard. See the accompanying fix PR.

	  Only error-severity findings gate merge (the pr.yaml `inspectcode` job
	  counts SARIF level=="error"), so nothing here weakens the gate.
	-->

	<!-- PublicApiAnalyzers (RS0016 286 alerts, RS0037 138 — 72% of the original 589).
	     EVIDENCE: InspectCode runs the Roslyn analyzers without passing
	     PublicAPI.Shipped.txt / PublicAPI.Unshipped.txt as AdditionalFiles, so the
	     analyzer believes nothing is declared and flags every public member. The
	     real build disagrees:
	         dotnet build src/Wolfgang.Etl.Xml/Wolfgang.Etl.Xml.csproj -c Release \
	             -p:TreatWarningsAsErrors=true
	     emits ZERO RS0016/RS0037. Enforcement genuinely lives in the build, where
	     RS0017 is active and validates the manifest against the real surface.
	     RS0026 is the same analyzer family and is included for consistency; it is
	     not currently firing. -->
	<s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=RS0016/@EntryIndexedValue">DO_NOT_SHOW</s:String>
	<s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=RS0037/@EntryIndexedValue">DO_NOT_SHOW</s:String>
	<s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=RS0026/@EntryIndexedValue">DO_NOT_SHOW</s:String>

	<!-- UnusedAutoPropertyAccessor.Global (20 alerts).
	     EVIDENCE: every site is a DTO whose properties are read by XmlSerializer
	     through REFLECTION, which R# cannot see — BenchmarkPerson, WidgetRecord,
	     Person, GcProfileWorkload.Record, MetricProbe. They are populated by object
	     initialisers in code and consumed by the serializer, so removing an accessor
	     would silently change the emitted XML contract. The one src/ site is the
	     RequiresUnreferencedCodeAttribute polyfill, whose surface must mirror the
	     framework type it stands in for. -->
	<s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=UnusedAutoPropertyAccessor_002EGlobal/@EntryIndexedValue">DO_NOT_SHOW</s:String>

	<!-- ConditionIsAlwaysTrueOrFalseAccordingToNullableAPIContract (2 remaining).
	     EVIDENCE: both are null-guards on the result of a USER-SUPPLIED factory
	     delegate in XmlMultiStreamLoader. The nullable annotation is a compile-time
	     claim, not a runtime guarantee — a caller can and does return null. Both
	     branches are reachable and covered by PASSING tests that supply exactly
	     that:
	         LoadAsync_when_stream_factory_returns_null_throws_InvalidOperationException
	             -> new XmlMultiStreamLoader<PersonRecord>(_ => (Stream)null!)
	         XmlLoaderBufferWriterTests
	             -> new XmlMultiStreamLoader<PersonRecord>(_ => (IBufferWriter<byte>)null!)
	     Deleting the guards on the analyser's advice would turn a clear
	     InvalidOperationException into a NullReferenceException.
	     NOTE: the third instance of this rule was a genuinely redundant guard in a
	     stress test and was FIXED, not covered by this entry. -->
	<s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=ConditionIsAlwaysTrueOrFalseAccordingToNullableAPIContract/@EntryIndexedValue">DO_NOT_SHOW</s:String>
</wpf:ResourceDictionary>
